.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES ASA USER CHANGE-PASSWORD" "1" "2026-09-02" "0.41.0" "sccfm-cli inventory devices asa user change-password Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-asa\-user\-change-password \- Change a local user password on ASA...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices asa user change-password
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a local user password on ASA devices (with verification).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-device\-name TEXT
Device name to search for (supports wildcards like 'branch-*').
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-query TEXT
Filter devices by a Lucene query.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-limit INTEGER RANGE
Maximum records to return  [default: 50; 1<=x<=200]
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-offset INTEGER RANGE
Pagination offset  [default: 0; x>=0]
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-device\-uids TEXT
List of device UIDs to target.
.TP
\fB\-\-username\fP TEXT
The local ASA username whose password will be changed.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-password,\fP \-\-password TEXT
The new password to set.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without performing the operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
